// osprey: flavor=ml
// ML twin of tuple_value_and_type_spelling.ospo. Pins [TYPE-TUPLE]
// (docs/specs/0004) in this flavor: the tuple PATTERN `(n, s)` is implemented
// as the positional row spelling, but the standalone tuple VALUE is not, and
// neither is `(int, string)` as a signature type.
//
// The distinction matters because ML parenthesises FLAT PARAMETERS with the
// same comma syntax ([FLAVOR-ML-CURRY], docs/specs/0024), so a tuple value is
// the one place the two spellings collide. Nothing pinned that boundary.
pair = (1, "a")

takesTuple : (int, string) -> string
takesTuple p = "unreachable"

print "unreachable"
